No, it's not automatically safe — but Tailwind v4 has a solution for exactly this.

Per `src/docs/upgrade-guide.mdx` §"Using a prefix": Tailwind v4 dropped the old `--tw-*` internal-only prefixing, but you can opt into prefixing **all** generated theme/utility CSS variables (not just utility classes) by writing:

```css
@import "tailwindcss" prefix(tw);
```

This namespaces both your custom `@theme` variables and Tailwind's built-in ones (e.g. `--tw-color-avocado-100`), so utilities like `rounded-lg` still work but won't leak/collide with your library consumers' own `--color-*`/`--radius-*` variables. This is the recommended approach for exactly your library-authoring scenario.

